  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, OVERSTATED (code read; diverging the rules needs a malformed shipped file). Refs: taint.py:2334 (requires explicit builtin), verify_claims.py:2310-2315 (shipped and not community), taint.py:2526 split_community_files, io_boundary.py:2472-2475 (path-or-line; decides COMMUNITY, not builtin); axis comment io_boundary.py:2242; non-empty-only validator :2273; PROVENANCE_BUILTIN still unreferenced (yaml_catalogs.py:278); the CI gate keeping the rules in agreement is tests/test_catalogue_scope_gates.py:763. Correction: the DefaultOverlay.provenance FIELD is display-only (sole reader verify_claims.py:2503); what is parsed as an enum is the raw YAML key (yaml_catalogs.py:288 overlay_declares_community, catalogues_doc.py:112, taint.py:2334). Real defects: the axis comment calls the value a 'prose citation' when it is the tier token (declare bounded-enum), the validator accepts any non-empty value, and three predicates exist where one should. The supply-chain tier-1 'unclassified' sentinel half is unrelated to catalogue provenance and is already tracked in WI-lidig (F78.A3 watch-item); refs moved there (cli.py:12072-12077, analyze/base.py:2008-2011). P3 -> P4: latent, held by a CI gate, nothing user-visible wrong today."  # 8ba7
